#. macro: <if $gn7><noun-en ObjStr 2 $gn7 1 1><else>{$gs2}</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 7 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <noun-en ObjStr 2 $gn7 1 1> — an English noun from a game data sheet, with article and number; sheet = ObjStr, form = 2, row = global number 7, count = 1, case = 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($gs1 == $gs2)>land<else>lands</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global text 1 (the name of the player character) == global text 2 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($n4 == 1)><noun-en Item 1 $n1 1 1><else><num $n4> <noun-en Item 3 $n1 $n4 1></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 4 == 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <noun-en Item 1 $n1 1 1> — an English noun from a game data sheet, with article and number; sheet = Item, form = 1, row = number parameter 1, count = 1, case = 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $n4> — a number; value = number parameter 4 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <noun-en Item 3 $n1 $n4 1> — an English noun from a game data sheet, with article and number; sheet = Item, form = 3, row = number parameter 1, count = number parameter 4, case = 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $n2> — a number; value = number parameter 2 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $n3> — a number; value = number parameter 3 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
